{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2158-01-20 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I'm Dr. Lee, one of the surgery team doctors. You're here because there are two aneurysms on your left arm fistula that need to be repaired."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2158-01-20 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve had this fistula for years. I noticed the bulge getting bigger. Is it dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2158-01-20 08:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be. Aneurysms can weaken the wall and might burst or cause poor blood flow. We plan to repair both today and also fix a narrow spot upstream."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2158-01-20 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I still be able to use it for dialysis after?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2158-01-20 08:06:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s the goal. We’ll do a patch venoplasty to keep the blood flow strong. You’ll go to the operating room in a few hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2158-01-20 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. I’ve had so many procedures, but this one feels important."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2158-01-20 08:09:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It is. We’ll take good care of you. Your medical history is complex, so we’re watching everything closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2158-01-20 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, we just got back from surgery. The repair of both aneurysms went well, and we did a patch to open up the narrowed area."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2158-01-20 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "How do I feel? I’m a bit groggy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2158-01-20 12:33:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s normal after anesthesia. You’re stable. The fistula has a good thrill and bruit, which means blood is flowing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2158-01-20 12:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I felt some pain before, but now it’s okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2158-01-20 12:36:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you on pain meds as needed. We’re also watching for fever, since you’ve had infections in the past."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2158-01-20 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs came back. White count is a bit low at 3.2, but your hemoglobin is stable. We’re keeping an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2158-01-20 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that because of my lupus or dialysis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2158-01-20 16:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Could be both. Lupus can affect blood counts, and so can chronic kidney disease. But we don’t see any signs of active infection now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2158-01-21 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You had a low-grade fever overnight, but it’s gone now. We sent blood and urine cultures just in case."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2158-01-21 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Fever? Could it be from the surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2158-01-21 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. Post-op fevers are common and often not due to infection. But with your history, we’re being cautious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2158-01-21 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember when my transplant got infected. I don’t want that again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2158-01-21 07:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We remember that too. That’s why we’re monitoring closely. So far, no signs of infection at the surgical site."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2158-01-21 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your first blood culture came back — no growth. That’s a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2158-01-21 11:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So no bacteria in my blood?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2158-01-21 11:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not in that sample. We’ll wait for the others, but this is reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2158-01-21 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll have dialysis now. The team will use your fistula carefully after the repair."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2158-01-21 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt to use it so soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2158-01-21 12:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They’ll be gentle. The repair is strong, and it’s important to keep the fistula working well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2158-01-21 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Two more blood cultures — both negative. That’s excellent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2158-01-21 17:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the fever wasn’t an infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2158-01-21 17:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not likely. It could have been a normal post-op reaction. You’re afebrile now and feeling better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2158-01-21 17:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the chest X-ray they did?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2158-01-21 17:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It showed your heart size has improved, possibly from less fluid. Lungs are clear — no pneumonia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2158-01-21 17:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I’ve had pleural effusions before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2158-01-21 17:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we’re watching that. But today’s X-ray looks stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2158-01-22 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news — you’re doing well. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2158-01-22 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Already? What about the urine culture?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2158-01-22 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It came back with mixed bacteria, but it looks like contamination from skin or genital area — not a real infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2158-01-22 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So no antibiotics needed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2158-01-22 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not for that. We’ll keep you on your regular meds and send you home with instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2158-01-22 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What should I watch for at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2158-01-22 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call the access clinic if you have fever over 101, pain, bleeding, or if the thrill in your arm disappears."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2158-01-22 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And no heavy lifting with this arm, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2158-01-22 08:14:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. No tight clothes or blood pressure checks on that side either."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2158-01-22 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll be careful. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2158-01-22 08:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Keep up with your dialysis and follow-up. You’re in good shape."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2158-01-22 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad this is behind me. It’s been a long road with my kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2158-01-22 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We know. But your fistula is repaired, and that’s a big win. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2158-01-22 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a final check — your fistula still has a strong thrill, and you’re afebrile. We’ll get your discharge papers ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2158-01-22 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel ready to go home. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2158-01-22 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Call if anything changes. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2158-01-22 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. See you at follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2158-01-20 00:49:00",
    "admission_end": "2158-01-22 16:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A female patient with end-stage renal disease was admitted for surgical revision of two aneurysms on her left arm arteriovenous fistula and patch venoplasty for outflow stenosis. The procedure was performed successfully on 2158-01-20. Postoperatively, she experienced intermittent low-grade fever, but blood cultures were negative and the fever resolved by discharge. A urine culture showed mixed flora consistent with contamination, not infection. She remained stable, with a functioning fistula exhibiting good thrill and bruit. She was discharged home in good condition with instructions to monitor for access site complications and continue outpatient dialysis.",
    "problems": [
      "Other complications due to renal dialysis device, implant, and graft",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease, unspecified, with chronic kidney disease stage V or end stage renal disease",
      "Unspecified pleural effusion",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Acquired absence of kidney",
      "Epilepsy, unspecified, without mention of intractable epilepsy",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Renal dialysis status"
    ]
  }
}
